<title>USA: US lawmaker to introduce stox trade bill Thursday.</title>
<headline>US lawmaker to introduce stox trade bill Thursday.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Reps. Michael Oxley (R-Ohio) and Edward Markey (D-Mass.) of the House Commerce Committee say they will introduce a bill Thursday to require stocks to be traded in dollars and cents, rather than the current increment of 1/8th of a dollar.</p>
<p>The sponsors say decimal pricing will lower transaction costs. They have scheduled a news conference to announce details of the bill.</p>
</text>
